From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Check the indexed contact manager size where it can
 hold

PxsIndexedContactManager is asserted to be a multiple of 16 bytes on
everything that is not x86-64, and on 32-bit x86 it is 24, so the Android
x86 build stops in every translation unit that reaches PxsIslandSim.h.
The i386 ABI aligns a PxU64 to 4 rather than to 8, which packs the base
class into 20 bytes instead of 24 and leaves room for the derived class
to put its 4 byte pointer in the base's tail padding. The other 32-bit
ABIs align it to 8 and land on 32 as they should, so armv7 and
WebAssembly satisfy the assertion and only x86 does not:

               PxsIndexedInteraction  PxsIndexedContactManager
  i686                  20                     24
  armv7, arm64, x86-64  24                     32

PhysX 4.1 met the assertion everywhere because PxsNodeType was an
articulation handle, one pointer wide, so the whole thing came to 16
bytes on a 32-bit platform. PhysX 5 made it a PxU64 and kept the
assertion, which nothing but x86-64 had been built with.

Nothing depends on the size: these live in a PxArray and are read through
their members, sorted by pointer, and never loaded a vector at a time or
walked with a stride of their own. The comment above the class says the
padding is waste that should go. So leave the assertion for the
architectures whose alignment can satisfy it, rather than pad the class
out on the one platform where a physics array would notice 8 more bytes
an element. PhysX counts emscripten as x86, so the check stops there as
well, on an ABI that does satisfy it.
---
 .../PhysX/source/lowlevel/software/include/PxsIslandManagerTypes.h     | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/lowlevel/software/include/PxsIslandManagerTypes.h b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/lowlevel/software/include/PxsIslandManagerTypes.h
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/lowlevel/software/include/PxsIslandManagerTypes.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/lowlevel/software/include/PxsIslandManagerTypes.h
@@ -133,7 +133,8 @@ struct PxsIndexedContactManager : public PxsIndexedInteraction	// 32
 	
 	PxsIndexedContactManager(PxsContactManager* cm) : contactManager(cm) {}
 };
-#if !PX_X64
+// 32-bit x86 aligns a PxU64 to 4, which packs the base class into 20 bytes and this one into 24
+#if !PX_X64 && !PX_X86
 PX_COMPILE_TIME_ASSERT(0==(sizeof(PxsIndexedContactManager) & 0x0f));
 #endif
 
